1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,353
Pay your credit card

2
00:00:01,353 --> 00:00:02,706
in full every month,

3
00:00:02,706 --> 00:00:04,059
never carry a balance?

4
00:00:04,059 --> 00:00:05,413
The card company is

5
00:00:05,413 --> 00:00:06,766
still making money off

6
00:00:06,766 --> 00:00:07,104
you.

7
00:00:07,104 --> 00:00:08,568
Every swipe triggers a

8
00:00:08,568 --> 00:00:10,031
small fee the merchant

9
00:00:10,031 --> 00:00:11,495
pays, called an interchange

10
00:00:11,495 --> 00:00:11,861
fee.

11
00:00:11,861 --> 00:00:13,141
That fee is split

12
00:00:13,141 --> 00:00:14,421
between your bank and

13
00:00:14,421 --> 00:00:15,701
the card network. It

14
00:00:15,701 --> 00:00:16,981
gets paid on every

15
00:00:16,981 --> 00:00:18,261
purchase, no matter when

16
00:00:18,261 --> 00:00:19,541
or how you pay

17
00:00:19,541 --> 00:00:20,181
your bill.

18
00:00:20,181 --> 00:00:21,594
That's why stores accept

19
00:00:21,594 --> 00:00:23,008
cards at all, and

20
00:00:23,008 --> 00:00:24,421
why some add a

21
00:00:24,421 --> 00:00:25,834
surcharge on small purchases.

22
00:00:25,834 --> 00:00:27,207
So the rewards, the

23
00:00:27,207 --> 00:00:28,579
points, the cash back

24
00:00:28,579 --> 00:00:29,952
— a share of

25
00:00:29,952 --> 00:00:31,325
that is funded by

26
00:00:31,325 --> 00:00:32,354
interchange, collected from

27
00:00:32,354 --> 00:00:32,697
every

28
00:00:32,697 --> 00:00:33,727
purchase you make.

29
00:00:33,727 --> 00:00:35,178
Paying in full still

30
00:00:35,178 --> 00:00:36,628
avoids interest. It just

31
00:00:36,628 --> 00:00:38,079
doesn't make the transaction

32
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,530
free for everyone else

33
00:00:39,530 --> 00:00:40,981
in the chain. Follow

34
00:00:40,981 --> 00:00:41,706
for more.
